@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<section class="py-4">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="mb-3">Constraints and LLM Parameters</h1>
        <p class="lead">Use constraints and parameter tuning to guide large language models toward predictable results. This section highlights common levers and when to use them.</p>

        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h2 class="h4">Prompt-level Constraints</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Length:</strong> “Answer in 3 bullet points” or “Limit to 100 words”.</li>
                            <li><strong>Format:</strong> JSON schemas, tables, markdown headings.</li>
                            <li><strong>Tone and persona:</strong> “You are a patient teacher.”</li>
                            <li><strong>Guardrails:</strong> “If unsure, respond with ‘Not enough information’.”</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h2 class="h4">Model Parameters</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Temperature:</strong> Lower for deterministic answers, higher for creativity.</li>
                            <li><strong>Top P / Top K:</strong> Control sampling diversity when exploring ideas.</li>
                            <li><strong>Max Tokens:</strong> Cap response length to avoid runaway outputs.</li>
                            <li><strong>Frequency / Presence Penalties:</strong> Reduce repetition or encourage new topics.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mt-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h4">Checklist Before Sending a Prompt</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Have you stated the desired format and length?</li>
                    <li>Do you describe a fallback when the model lacks information?</li>
                    <li>Are parameter settings aligned with the task (precision vs. creativity)?</li>
                    <li>Is there sensitive content that needs filtering or redaction?</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
